ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1
==================================================
February 1 is the 32nd day of the year in the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] ;  333 days remain until the end of the year (334 in  [LINK: (leap years) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_year] ).


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (1327) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1327]  – The teenaged  [LINK: (Edward III) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_III]  is crowned King of England, but the country is ruled by his mother  [LINK: (Queen Isabella) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabella_of_France]  and her lover  [LINK: (Roger Mortimer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Mortimer,_1st_Earl_of_March] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (1411) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1411]  – The  [LINK: (First Peace of Thorn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Thorn_(1411)]  is signed in  [LINK: (Thorn (Toruń)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toru%C5%84] ,  [LINK: (Monastic State of the Teutonic Knights) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monastic_State_of_the_Teutonic_Knights]  (Prussia). [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-2]

[LINK: (1662) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1662]  – The Chinese general  [LINK: (Koxinga) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koxinga]  seizes the island of  [LINK: (Taiwan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan]  after a  [LINK: (nine-month siege) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Fort_Zeelandia] . [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (1713) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1713]  – The Kalabalik or  [LINK: (Skirmish at Bender) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skirmish_at_Bender]  results from the Ottoman Sultan  [LINK: (Ahmed III) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmed_III] 's order that his unwelcome guest, King  [LINK: (Charles XII of Sweden) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XII_of_Sweden] , be seized. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (1793) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1793]  –  [LINK: (French Revolutionary Wars) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Revolutionary_Wars] : France declares war on the United Kingdom and the Netherlands.

[LINK: (1796) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1796]  – The capital of  [LINK: (Upper Canada) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upper_Canada]  is moved from  [LINK: (Newark) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newark,_Upper_Canada]  to  [LINK: (York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/York,_Upper_Canada] .

[LINK: (1814) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1814]  –  [LINK: (Mayon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayon]  in the  [LINK: (Philippines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippines]  erupts, killing around 1,200 people, which was the most devastating eruption of the volcano.

[LINK: (1835) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1835]  –  [LINK: (Slavery is abolished) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abolition_of_slavery]  in  [LINK: (Mauritius) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauritius] . [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-5]

[LINK: (1861) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1861]  –  [LINK: (American Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War] :  [LINK: (Texas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas]   [LINK: (secedes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_in_the_American_Civil_War#Seccession]  from the United States and joins the  [LINK: (Confederacy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Confederate_States_of_America]  a week later.

[LINK: (1864) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1864]  –  [LINK: (Second Schleswig War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Schleswig_War] : Prussian forces crossed the border into Schleswig, starting the war. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (1865) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1865]  – President  [LINK: (Abraham Lincoln) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham_Lincoln]  signs the  [LINK: (Thirteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thirteenth_Amendment_to_the_United_States_Constitution] .

[LINK: (1884) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1884]  – The first volume (A to Ant) of the  [LINK: (Oxford English Dictionary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford_English_Dictionary]  is published. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-7]

[LINK: (1893) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1893]  –  [LINK: (Thomas A. Edison) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_A._Edison]  finishes construction of the first  [LINK: (motion picture studio) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motion_picture_studio] , the  [LINK: (Black Maria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edison%27s_Black_Maria]  in  [LINK: (West Orange, New Jersey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Orange,_New_Jersey] . [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (1895) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1895]  –  [LINK: (Fountains Valley, Pretoria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountains_Valley,_Pretoria] , the oldest  [LINK: (nature reserve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature_reserve]  in Africa, is proclaimed by President  [LINK: (Paul Kruger) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Kruger] .

[LINK: (1896) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1896]  –  [LINK: (La bohème) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_boh%C3%A8me]  premieres in Turin at the  [LINK: (Teatro Regio (Turin)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teatro_Regio_(Turin)] , conducted by the young  [LINK: (Arturo Toscanini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arturo_Toscanini] .

[LINK: (1897) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1897]  –  [LINK: (Shinhan Bank) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinhan_Bank] , the  [LINK: (oldest bank in South Korea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_banks_in_South_Korea] , opens in  [LINK: (Seoul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seoul] .

[LINK: (1900) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1900]  – Great Britain, defeated by Boers in key battles, names  [LINK: (Lord Roberts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_Roberts,_1st_Earl_Roberts]  commander of British forces in South Africa. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (1908) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1908]  –  [LINK: (Lisbon Regicide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisbon_Regicide] : King  [LINK: (Carlos I of Portugal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlos_I_of_Portugal]  and  [LINK: (Infante Luis Filipe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lu%C3%ADs_Filipe,_Prince_Royal_of_Portugal]  are shot dead in  [LINK: (Lisbon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisbon] . [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-10]

[LINK: (1924) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1924]  –  [LINK: (Russia–United Kingdom relations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia%E2%80%93United_Kingdom_relations]  are restored, over six years after the Communist revolution. [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-11]

[LINK: (1942) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1942]  –  [LINK: (World War II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II] :  [LINK: (Josef Terboven) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josef_Terboven] ,  [LINK: (Reichskommissar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reichskommissar]  of  [LINK: (German-occupied Norway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_occupation_of_Norway] , appoints  [LINK: (Vidkun Quisling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vidkun_Quisling]  the  [LINK: (Minister President) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Norway]  of the  [LINK: (National Government) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quisling_regime] .

1942   – World War II: U.S. Navy conducts  [LINK: (Marshalls–Gilberts raids) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshalls%E2%80%93Gilberts_raids] , the first offensive action by the United States against Japanese forces in the  [LINK: (Pacific Theater) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Ocean_theater_of_World_War_II] . [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-12]

1942   –  [LINK: (Voice of America) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voice_of_America] , the official external radio and television service of the  [LINK: (United States government) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_government_of_the_United_States] , begins broadcasting with programs aimed at areas controlled by the  [LINK: (Axis powers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axis_powers] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-13]

1942 –  [LINK: (Mao Zedong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mao_Zedong]  makes a speech on "Reform in Learning, the Party and Literature", which puts into motion the  [LINK: (Yan'an Rectification Movement) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yan%27an_Rectification_Movement] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-14]

[LINK: (1946) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1946]  –  [LINK: (Trygve Lie) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trygve_Lie]  of Norway is picked to be the first  [LINK: (United Nations Secretary-General) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Secretary-General] . [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-15]

1946 – The  [LINK: (Parliament of Hungary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Assembly_(Hungary)]  abolishes the monarchy after nine centuries, and proclaims the  [LINK: (Hungarian Republic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Hungarian_Republic] . [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-16]

[LINK: (1950) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1950]  – The first prototype of the  [LINK: (MiG-17) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikoyan-Gurevich_MiG-17]  makes its maiden flight. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-17]

[LINK: (1957) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1957]  –  [LINK: (Northeast Airlines Flight 823) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northeast_Airlines_Flight_823]  crashes on  [LINK: (Rikers Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rikers_Island]  in  [LINK: (New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City] , killing 20 people and injuring 78 others. [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-18]

[LINK: (1960) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960]  – Four black students stage the first of the  [LINK: (Greensboro sit-ins) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greensboro_sit-ins]  at a lunch counter in  [LINK: (Greensboro, North Carolina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greensboro,_North_Carolina] . [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-19]

[LINK: (1964) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1964]  –  [LINK: (The Beatles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles]  have their first number one hit in the United States with " [LINK: (I Want to Hold Your Hand) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Want_to_Hold_Your_Hand] ". [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-20]

[LINK: (1968) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] : The execution of  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  officer  [LINK: (Nguyễn Văn Lém) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saigon_Execution]  by  [LINK: (South Vietnamese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam]  National Police Chief  [LINK: (Nguyễn Ngọc Loan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nguy%E1%BB%85n_Ng%E1%BB%8Dc_Loan]  is recorded on motion picture film, as well as in an iconic still photograph taken by  [LINK: (Eddie Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Adams_(photographer)] . [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-21]

1968 – Canada's three military services, the  [LINK: (Royal Canadian Navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Canadian_Navy] , the  [LINK: (Canadian Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Army]  and the  [LINK: (Royal Canadian Air Force) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Canadian_Air_Force] , are unified into the  [LINK: (Canadian Forces) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Forces] . [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-22]

1968 – The  [LINK: (New York Central Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Central_Railroad]  and the  [LINK: (Pennsylvania Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Railroad]  are merged to form  [LINK: (Penn Central Transportation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penn_Central_Transportation] .

[LINK: (1972) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1972]  –  [LINK: (Kuala Lumpur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuala_Lumpur]  becomes a city by a royal charter granted by the  [LINK: (Yang di-Pertuan Agong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_of_Malaysia]  of  [LINK: (Malaysia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malaysia] . [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-23]

[LINK: (1974) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1974]  –  [LINK: (A fire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joelma_Building_fire]  in the 25-story  [LINK: (Joelma Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joelma_Building]  in  [LINK: (São Paulo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Paulo] , Brazil kills 189 and injures 293.

[LINK: (1979) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1979]  –  [LINK: (Iranian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran]   [LINK: (Ayatollah) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayatollah]   [LINK: (Ruhollah Khomeini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruhollah_Khomeini]   [LINK: (returns) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruhollah_Khomeini%27s_return_to_Iran]  to  [LINK: (Tehran) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tehran]  after nearly 15 years of exile. [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-24]

[LINK: (1981) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1981]  – The  [LINK: (Underarm bowling incident of 1981) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underarm_bowling_incident_of_1981]  occurred when  [LINK: (Trevor Chappell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Chappell]  bowls underarm on the final delivery of a game between  [LINK: (Australia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_men%27s_national_cricket_team]  and  [LINK: (New Zealand) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Zealand_men%27s_national_cricket_team]  at the  [LINK: (Melbourne Cricket Ground) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melbourne_Cricket_Ground]  (MCG). [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-25]

[LINK: (1991) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991]  – A runway  [LINK: (collision) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Los_Angeles_runway_collision]  between USAir Flight 1493 and SkyWest Flight 5569 at  [LINK: (Los Angeles International Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles_International_Airport]  results in the deaths of 34 people, and injuries to 30 others. [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-26]

[LINK: (1991) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991]  – A  [LINK: (magnitude 6.8 earthquake) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991_Hindu_Kush_earthquake]  strikes the  [LINK: (Hindu Kush) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindu_Kush]  region, killing at least 848 people in Afghanistan, Pakistan and present-day Tajikistan. [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-27]

[LINK: (1992) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992]  – The Chief Judicial Magistrate of  [LINK: (Bhopal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhopal]  court declares  [LINK: (Warren Anderson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_Anderson_(American_businessman)] , ex- [LINK: (CEO) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_executive_officer]  of  [LINK: (Union Carbide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Carbide] , a fugitive under Indian law for failing to appear in the  [LINK: (Bhopal disaster) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhopal_disaster]  case. [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-28]

[LINK: (1996) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996]  – The  [LINK: (Communications Decency Act) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Communications_Decency_Act]  is passed by the  [LINK: (U.S. Congress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Congress] . [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-29]

[LINK: (1998) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1998]  – Rear Admiral  [LINK: (Lillian E. Fishburne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lillian_E._Fishburne]  becomes the first female African American to be promoted to rear admiral. [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-30]

[LINK: (2002) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002]  –  [LINK: (Daniel Pearl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Pearl] , American journalist and South Asia Bureau Chief of  [LINK: (The Wall Street Journal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wall_Street_Journal] , kidnapped on January 23, is beheaded and mutilated by his captors. [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-31]

[LINK: (2003) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2003]  –  [LINK: (Space Shuttle Columbia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle_Columbia]   [LINK: (disintegrated during the reentry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle_Columbia_disaster]  of mission  [LINK: (STS-107) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STS-107]  into the Earth's atmosphere, killing all seven astronauts aboard. [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-32]

[LINK: (2004) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2004]  –  [LINK: (Hajj pilgrimage stampede) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidents_during_the_Hajj#Failures_in_crowd_control] : In a stampede at the  [LINK: (Hajj) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hajj]  pilgrimage in  [LINK: (Saudi Arabia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia] , 251 people are trampled to death and 244 injured. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-33]

2004   –  [LINK: (Double suicide attack in Erbil) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2004_Erbil_bombings]  on the offices of  [LINK: (Iraqi Kurdish) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraqi_Kurdistan]  political parties by members of  [LINK: (Jama'at al-Tawhid wal-Jihad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jama%27at_al-Tawhid_wal-Jihad]  [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-34]

[LINK: (2005) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2005]  – King  [LINK: (Gyanendra of Nepal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gyanendra_of_Nepal]  carries out a  [LINK: (coup d'état) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coup_d%27%C3%A9tat]  to capture the democracy, becoming Chairman of the Councils of ministers. [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-35]

[LINK: (2007) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007]  – The  [LINK: (National Weather Service) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Weather_Service]  in the  [LINK: (United States) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States]  switches from the  [LINK: (Fujita scale) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujita_scale]  to the new  [LINK: (Enhanced Fujita scale) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_Fujita_scale]  to measure the intensity and strength of tornadoes. [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-36]

[LINK: (2009) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009]  – The  [LINK: (first cabinet of Jóhanna Sigurðardóttir) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_cabinet_of_J%C3%B3hanna_Sigur%C3%B0ard%C3%B3ttir]  was formed in  [LINK: (Iceland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceland] , making  [LINK: (her) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%B3hanna_Sigur%C3%B0ard%C3%B3ttir]  the country's first female prime minister and the world's first openly  [LINK: (gay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LGBTQ_people]  head of government. [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-37]

[LINK: (2012) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012]  – Seventy-four people are killed and over 500 injured as a result of  [LINK: (clashes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Said_Stadium_riot]  between fans of Egyptian football teams  [LINK: (Al Masry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Masry_SC]  and  [LINK: (Al Ahly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Ahly_SC]  in the city of  [LINK: (Port Said) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Said] . [LINK: ([38]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-38]

[LINK: (2013) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013]  –  [LINK: (The Shard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shard] , the  [LINK: (sixth-tallest building in Europe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tallest_buildings_in_Europe] , opens its viewing gallery to the public. [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-39]

[LINK: (2021) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021]  – A  [LINK: (coup d'état) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Myanmar_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat]  in  [LINK: (Myanmar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myanmar]  removes  [LINK: (Aung San Suu Kyi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aung_San_Suu_Kyi]  from power and restores military rule. [LINK: ([40]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-40]

[LINK: (2022) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022]  – Five-year-old Moroccan boy  [LINK: (Rayan Aourram) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Rayan_Aourram]  falls into a 32-meter (105 feet) deep well in Ighran village in  [LINK: (Tamorot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamorot]  commune,  [LINK: (Chefchaouen Province) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chefchaouen_Province] , Morocco, but dies four days later, before rescue workers reached him. [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1#cite_note-41]


